OL,3,GNEWSAThames Water says hosepipe ban
OL,4,Acould last months yet
OL,5,
OL,6,FA hosepipe ban will remain in place
OL,7,Facross the area served by Thames Water
OL,8,Funtil there is sustained rainfall over
OL,9,Fweeks or perhaps months, the company
OL,10,Fhas said.
OL,12,FThe ban introduced on 23 July has not
OL,13,Fbeen enough to fill up reservoirs, with
OL,14,Frecent rainfall still below the
OL,15,Flong-term average.
OL,17,FThe restriction means 10.1 million
OL,18,Fcustomers should not use hosepipes to
OL,19,Fwater gardens, clean cars, fill
OL,20,Fpaddling pools or swimming pools, or
OL,21,Fclean windows.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
